Z||000000||Songman||04-07-2001||12:27 AM||||Cliff, you may want to close this one too...<P>I thought this forum was for opinions. And I thought that even controversial ideas were welcome so people could express their real feelings. I have not seen any bad things happen over someone expressing their feelings here, even if they are not held by the majority of the forum. That is makes the world go around...<P>On the other thread, someone said that people would be afraid to post their opinions because people might stop talking to them, etc... I think if someone will go back and read my post, I stated my opinion very well. I'm sure not all people agreed with it, but I believe in it enough to say it out loud. I called prejudice exactly what it is, and said that it comes in all forms. If anyone doesn't like it, they don't have to talk to me. I believe what I believe.<P>In my opinion, if you do not believe in something enough to be held accountable for speaking up on it's behalf, you don't really believe in it too much.<P>For the most part I think we are all adults here. We should have learned that everyone had different lifestyles and beliefs and that there is room on this Earth for all of us. Anyone that hasn't learned that.. those are the people that get offended by people asking a controversial question.<P>Personally, I think it was a mistake to close the other thread because someone didn't like what it 'might' say. But this is not my forum and I respect Cliff for doing what he thinks. But over 2000 people had the ability to stand up for their own views. Most chose not to and that is their right. But the ones of us that did also have the right to be heard. If you read my posts on subjects like this during my time here, you will see that I always believe in people's rights. <P>That is my opinion and I am proud of it. Thanks for listening.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
